    "blocks_tibAtJ": {
      "type": "_blocks",
      "blocks": {
        "ai_gen_block_0029bb1_KcYBnV": {
          "type": "ai_gen_block_0029bb1",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "How does the diamond carat weight scale work?",
            "text": "<p>The diamond carat weight scale measures a diamond’s weight, with one carat divided into 100 points for accuracy. For instance, a 0.50 carat diamond is equivalent to 50 points, while a 1.00 carat diamond equals 100 points. This system allows for precise comparison between stones of different sizes.</p><p>Carat weight can range from very small fractions of a carat through to exceptionally large, rare stones, with certain ranges more commonly seen in fine jewellery.</p><p><strong>Less than 0.50 carats:</strong> Diamonds in this range are generally more subtle in scale and are often used as accent stones or for delicate, understated pieces.</p><p><strong>0.50 to 0.99 carats: </strong>This range offers a balanced size with noticeable presence, making it a popular choice for those seeking a refined centre stone without reaching the one carat threshold.</p><p><strong>1.00 to 1.99 carats: </strong>Diamonds within this range are often considered a classic benchmark for engagement rings, delivering strong visual impact while remaining relatively accessible.</p><p><strong>2.00 to 4.99 carats: </strong>Stones in this category are more substantial and increasingly rare, offering a more pronounced presence and typically commanding higher value.</p><p><strong>5.00 carats and above:</strong> Diamonds at this level are uncommon and highly sought after, often reserved for statement pieces and high jewellery due to their size and rarity.</p>",
            "heading_size_desktop": 30,
            "text_size_desktop": 18,
            "padding_left_desktop": 380,
            "padding_right_desktop": 380,
            "spacing_desktop": 40,
            "heading_size_mobile": 20,
            "text_size_mobile": 14,
            "padding_left_mobile": 40,
            "padding_right_mobile": 40,
            "spacing_mobile": 20,
            "text_alignment": "center",
            "heading_color": "#000000",
            "text_color": "#000000"
          },
          "blocks": {}
        }
      },
